Quantitative and technical literacy (@quantitative-literacy: 0, is #chapter, #quantitative-literacy "Reading-from-zero.lingua#r_0RVVPMXQQDS96N2BCGHD50N2NN") { r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2
Learn the numerical and spatial language used to read, question, and produce technical work. Begin from counts and ordinary arithmetic, then connect units, proportions, equations, graphs, geometry, drawings, flows, measurement, and increasingly demanding models. The same Records can support mining, chemistry, machinery, logistics, energy, electronics, and scientific research.

**Start:** [Begin quantitative and technical literacy from zero](Reading-from-zero.lingua#r_0RVVPMXQQDS96N2BCGHD50N2NN). Its reading progression begins with complete practical mathematics books and names the later textbook blocks. A reader with prior fluency can attempt the foundation review and follow the links back where needed.

| Part | Readings |
| --- | --- |
| Numerical foundation | [A number needs a quantity and a reference](foundations/Quantity-and-reference.lingua#r_65GAJ89AZRG6VYVXDC43NBT0DK) · [Counting, arithmetic, signs, and exact values](foundations/Whole-and-signed-numbers.lingua#r_0SJY2JGRVTKNRYW2N2QV64WXJ7) · [Fractions, decimals, rounding, and equivalent values](foundations/Fractions-and-decimals.lingua#r_0JEY0Y348N7B9FCFRMW0PQGDTD) · [Ratios, proportions, percentages, and denominators](foundations/Ratios-and-percentages.lingua#r_2VBAHXE0WMP7E6WA0NNKV1N31S) · [Exponents, scientific notation, and orders of magnitude](foundations/Powers-and-scale.lingua#r_55FCWM0V49GJXKV3YN0KYGE006) · [Units, dimensions, and equations that can make sense](foundations/Units-and-dimensions.lingua#r_3A511KGNX59K2YHKT83NM38NE1) · [Conversions, offsets, reference states, and compound units](foundations/Conversions-and-offsets.lingua#r_5WNAMEBVYKZM0TYN5A4TBYDSWD) |
| Equations, graphs, and space | [Equations, unknowns, systems, and constraints](foundations/Equations-and-constraints.lingua#r_2XGYVPEJSA3GYYV0K6PYXCHXVZ) · [Functions, tables, domains, and inverse questions](foundations/Functions-and-tables.lingua#r_0F4KMKK6ET8T22RG617S1RDZS2) · [Read graphs, interpolate, and question a visual claim](foundations/Graphs-and-interpolation.lingua#r_2GDCZSQKNW5BCGN7B5D9G36HK2) · [Exponential change and logarithmic scales](foundations/Exponential-and-logarithmic-scales.lingua#r_0NQPY7MA3SJ3TR97ZJRTW7ZQPG) · [Length, area, volume, density, and scaling a shape](foundations/Geometry-and-volume.lingua#r_6DCACA5A4YM1PC08DT5WEW3BHW) · [Angles, grade, triangles, and periodic relationships](foundations/Angles-and-trigonometry.lingua#r_0FPTH1YN87PZ97SHWGX19ZJZDZ) · [Vectors, coordinate systems, and spatial meaning](foundations/Vectors-and-projections.lingua#r_477P2M3HVZQ0PT56SF027VP68J) |
| Foundation review | [Bring the numerical and spatial foundation together](study/Foundation-review.lingua#r_66P3KR79E835QXT45SKDC2FWYY) |
| Drawings, quantities in processes, and observations | [Technical drawings — turn views into a spatial description](practice/Technical-drawings.lingua#r_3PEBG59JH06QGKQCR5YAKKF3R2) · [Dimensions, tolerances, references, and an inspection question](practice/Dimensions-and-tolerances.lingua#r_0K38T1TBRR4N9ESP1FYR55H90T) · [Rates, accumulation, and the boundary of an account](practice/Rates-and-accumulation.lingua#r_0NTXN5E5ZJ1A8C149BQF4G2YCZ) · [Mass and component balances — account for every stream](practice/Mass-and-component-balances.lingua#r_163GVDJGRJ1DD4JT2398GM371H) · [Yield, recovery, purity, and usable output](practice/Yield-and-recovery.lingua#r_2G5J64TBJZ1NBBT1DS2FT81B20) · [Concentrations, moisture, and changing the basis](practice/Concentrations-and-bases.lingua#r_0XCSBEG82Y6TYKX1Z28R693AY5) · [Energy, power, capacity, and a production denominator](practice/Energy-power-and-capacity.lingua#r_0EE7P9TMJK8SRVCVM1M7K61RAR) · [Keep observations, formulas, units, and revisions recoverable](practice/Data-and-calculation-records.lingua#r_5TTXVQ6161YYC7CFWDSQCV8WX8) · [Repeated observations, averages, spread, and shared errors](practice/Repeated-observations.lingua#r_6S7MZWJ6S5MERFKE0NQEWC5SY2) · [Measurement — resolution, variation, bias, and uncertainty](practice/Measurement-and-uncertainty.lingua#r_7ECX6WRYHP37YAMGXEBGYRW23X) · [Estimation, bounds, and the cost of a wrong assumption](practice/Estimates-and-bounds.lingua#r_5YGGH6Z676MZJNTQXTWQ8AJE4J) |
| Deeper model reasoning | [Scaling — what changes when a process becomes larger?](models/Scaling-and-similarity.lingua#r_5XVMAPM10GAFS130TFV3RH2YDK) · [Dimensionless groups and the limits of dimensional reasoning](models/Dimensionless-groups.lingua#r_7R4PTGBX4NTZWXQGPC09C1F7ZQ) · [Small changes, derivatives, and first-order approximations](models/Small-changes-and-derivatives.lingua#r_4T51QH8VRCNNMY5WD30VJS5P52) · [Sensitivity, cancellation, dependencies, and conditioning](models/Sensitivity-and-conditioning.lingua#r_43NVV3KJX9W9R026T1NKCYMP3T) · [Discretization — approximate a changing process and check it](models/Limits-and-discretization.lingua#r_5FA5RGRRQHG8P107F8AVJ2SGEX) · [What do the observations actually determine?](models/Observation-and-identifiability.lingua#r_5J7K2N4XB97BQSJBCXCMCJVC5W) |
| Independent studies and completion | [Read a technical claim all the way back to its quantities](study/Reading-a-technical-claim.lingua#r_2QQHDYD4PQCPQ2CQY3BC53MHP9) · [Study a material process from receipts to usable output](study/Stock-and-process-study.lingua#r_6AJ0D56F46SY1AFC4DGJXFD7RJ) · [Study a part from a drawing through a measurement report](study/Draw-and-measure-study.lingua#r_5T0JG8AMM1T2N0KY48SNYBHZ5Y) · [Follow a quantitative account across an infrastructure chain](study/Infrastructure-account.lingua#r_1SPNJTQF61CBZ3V6H0NPM7SD0E) · [Advanced study — derive, compare, test, and revise a model](study/Advanced-quantitative-study.lingua#r_6G38PYR8GVPZNZ16CNJ31VN259) · [What completing quantitative and technical literacy means](study/Completion.lingua#r_2C68EEJZH5KY4Z0DAPKBQEAAZ0) |


Read the linked explanations alongside the assigned books and articles. The short Records connect and question the readings; they do not replace hundreds of textbook pages with a summary. The material-process and drawing studies branch from the technical-claim reading and both contribute to the later infrastructure account. Other references remain available without becoming additional required steps.

**Depth:** completing this reading means independently explaining and checking technical quantities and derivations, reconstructing a published claim, producing a measurement and material-accounting study, and defending an advanced model investigation. [What completing quantitative and technical literacy means](study/Completion.lingua#r_2C68EEJZH5KY4Z0DAPKBQEAAZ0) states the evidence for that claim. It is a demanding foundation with advanced work, and detailed disciplinary study can reuse it rather than repeat it.

**Sources:** [Quantitative literacy sources — books, standards, and articles](Sources.lingua#r_7MMXWNA1B4YGA271KMHPPJEK9Q). Books and articles are linked through authorized external locations; no copies are bundled. Examples labelled hypothetical are supplied teaching data rather than industrial operating figures.

Return to [shared inquiry](../Inquiry.lingua#r_75MNKZQKNB0XBG021SWWW2HASB) or [Philosophy](../../../../scholazein/philosophy/Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001) when asking what counts as evidence, why a model abstracts particular features, or what a numerical conclusion leaves undetermined.

Follow these links directly, or select the Records at either endpoint of `#quantitative-literacy` assertions through an ordinary Protein. Sources and comparisons keep their own connections.
} r_4XVN56PQC13JGNFPV0CSGXDCZ2

